      {
         "id": "b",
         "prompt": "Find \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{g(x) - 3}{x^{2} - 1} \\). Show the work that leads to your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\frac{5}{2}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {"text": "g is continuous at 1 because it is differentiable, so both parts tend to 0.", "latex": "\\lim_{x\\to 1}(g(x) - 3) = 0, \\quad \\lim_{x\\to 1}(x^{2} - 1) = 0"},
            {"text": "Apply L'Hospital's Rule.", "latex": "\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{g'(x)}{2x} = \\frac{g'(1)}{2} = \\frac{5}{2}"}
